{"agent":"pm-kilo","data":{"body":"Today `ddflow next --phase P-perf-metrics` returns only the READY items that live INSIDE that phase. A phase at the tail of the critical path (P-perf-metrics) then shows '0 ready / 21 blocked' with no way to see — from the same command — which upstream dependencies are themselves ready to claim. Feature: by default `ddflow next --phase <id>` should ALSO include the phase's unmet dependencies' ready items (so a lane asked to drive a phase can start the upstream blockers first); an explicit parameter (e.g. `--phase-only` / `--no-deps` / `--scope phase`) restores the current in-phase-only behaviour. The default must not disguise the phase boundary: label each returned upstream item as a blocking-dependency, not an in-phase item.","globs":["ddflow/api/next.py","ddflow/services/next*.py","ddflow/surfaces/commands/next.py","tests/test_next*.py"],"line":"","needs":[],"older_ddflow":"0.2.10","parent":"P-completion","priority":80,"tags":["ddflow-self","feature","wave:0"],"title":"ddflow next --phase <id> returns only in-phase ready items, hiding the ready upstream dependencies that block the phase"},"id":"e0e35e3d62475e4dfd5fadc54","kind":"task.added","lamport":169680,"schema":1,"subject":"B-next-phase-hides-blocking-deps","ts":"2026-11-11T04:20:42.676546Z"}
